---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Slay the Spire 2 Co-op Guide &mdash; How Multiplayer Works"
  description="Complete Slay the Spire 2 co-op guide: how multiplayer works, core mechanics, enemy scaling, shared debuffs, revival rules, Mend, map voting, and 10 essential tips for 2-4 player runs."
>
  <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-amber-400 not-prose mb-6">
      Slay the Spire 2 Co-op Guide: How Multiplayer Works
    </h1>

    <p class="lead text-lg text-slate-300">
      Slay the Spire 2 introduces <strong>4-player online co-op</strong> for the first time in the series.
      Each player controls their own character with independent decks, but shares the map, enemies, and victory conditions.
      This guide covers everything you need to know about multiplayer mechanics.
    </p>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <nav class="not-prose bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700 my-8" aria-label="Table of Contents">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-400 mb-3">Table of Contents</h2>
      <ol class="text-sm space-y-1 text-slate-300 list-decimal list-inside">
        <li><a href="#getting-started" class="hover:text-amber-400">Getting Started</a></li>
        <li><a href="#core-mechanics" class="hover:text-amber-400">Core Multiplayer Mechanics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#death-revival" class="hover:text-amber-400">Death &amp; Revival</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rest-sites" class="hover:text-amber-400">Rest Sites &amp; Mend</a></li>
        <li><a href="#relic-drafting" class="hover:text-amber-400">Relic Drafting</a></li>
        <li><a href="#map-voting" class="hover:text-amber-400">Map Voting &amp; Pathing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#coop-cards" class="hover:text-amber-400">Co-op Exclusive Cards</a></li>
        <li><a href="#essential-tips" class="hover:text-amber-400">10 Essential Multiplayer Tips</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Section 1: Getting Started -->
    <section id="getting-started" class="scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">1. Getting Started</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2 not-prose">How to Start a Multiplayer Game</h3>
      <ol class="space-y-2 list-decimal list-outside ml-5">
        <li>Make sure you and your friends are <strong>Steam friends</strong></li>
        <li>From the main menu, choose <strong>Multiplayer</strong></li>
        <li>One player selects <strong>Host</strong>; everyone else selects <strong>Join</strong></li>
        <li>Each player picks a character — duplicates are allowed but <strong>not recommended</strong></li>
        <li>Save files can be shared or created fresh</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="not-prose bg-amber-900/30 border border-amber-600/40 rounded-lg p-4 my-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-300"><strong>Important:</strong> There is currently <strong>no matchmaking</strong> or local couch co-op. You can only play with Steam friends. The host must have a stable internet connection and stay connected for the entire run.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2 not-prose">Available Characters (Early Access)</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
        <li><strong class="text-red-400">Ironclad</strong> — Tank, self-healing, high HP, massive Block</li>
        <li><strong class="text-green-400">Silent</strong> — Debuffer, Poison DPS, applies Vulnerable/Weak for the team</li>
        <li><strong class="text-blue-400">Defect</strong> — Scaling DPS, Orb utility (Lightning/Frost/Plasma)</li>
        <li><strong class="text-purple-400">Necrobinder</strong> — Board control, off-tank (Osty bodyguard), Doom debuff</li>
        <li><strong class="text-yellow-400">Regent</strong> — Burst damage, Stars system for massive single-turn kills</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Core Mechanics -->
    <section id="core-mechanics" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">2. Core Multiplayer Mechanics</h2>

      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-slate-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-700">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">Mechanic</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">How It Works</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Enemy Scaling</td>
              <td class="p-3">Enemy HP and damage scale with the number of players. More players = beefier enemies. HP scales approximately +30% per additional player.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Shared Debuffs</td>
              <td class="p-3"><strong class="text-amber-300">This is the most important co-op mechanic.</strong> Vulnerable, Weak, Poison, and Doom applied by one player benefit the <em>entire team</em>. Poison and Doom bypass Block.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Simultaneous Turns</td>
              <td class="p-3">All players act at the same time. Communication is critical to avoid wasting resources — debuff first, then attack.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Individual Resources</td>
              <td class="p-3">Each player manages their own deck, relics, energy pool, and gold. Merchant inventory and card rewards are unique to each player.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Potions</td>
              <td class="p-3">"Throwing" potions can be used on teammates to heal or buff them. "Drink" potions are self-only. Save thrown potions for clutch saves.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Multiplayer Cards</td>
              <td class="p-3">Every character has co-op exclusive cards that don't appear in solo mode. These enable team Block sharing, ally buffs, attack redirection, and more.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-white whitespace-nowrap">Elite Rewards</td>
              <td class="p-3">Elites are even more rewarding in co-op — 4 relics distributed across the team from a single elite fight. Prioritize elites early.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Death & Revival -->
    <section id="death-revival" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">3. Death &amp; Revival</h2>

      <p>
        When a player's HP reaches zero during combat, they are <strong>knocked out</strong> — not permanently dead.
        The fight continues without them. After combat ends, if <strong>at least one teammate survives</strong>,
        all dead players automatically revive with <strong>1 HP</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        This "designated survivor" mechanic is the foundation of co-op survival strategy.
        Your tankiest character should always play conservatively when the team is low.
        A run only truly ends when <strong>every player falls</strong> in the same fight.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose bg-green-900/30 border border-green-600/40 rounded-lg p-4 my-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-green-300"><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Funnel defensive resources (Block cards, potions, relics) to your tank when things get dicey. One survivor = everyone revives.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Rest Sites & Mend -->
    <section id="rest-sites" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">4. Rest Sites &amp; Mend</h2>

      <p>
        Rest Sites (campfires) gain a <strong>third option</strong> in multiplayer beyond the normal "Rest" (heal self) and "Upgrade":
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2 not-prose">Mend — Heal a Teammate</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Mend</strong> allows you to sacrifice your own Rest action to heal <strong>another player for 30% of their maximum HP</strong>.
        This is a strategic trade-off: you give up your own heal or upgrade opportunity to keep a struggling teammate alive.
      </p>

      <ul class="space-y-1 mt-3">
        <li>Use Mend when a teammate revives with 1 HP after a tough fight — getting them back to safe HP range is more valuable than healing yourself</li>
        <li>The <strong>Miniature Tent</strong> relic is particularly strong in co-op, potentially allowing a double heal on an ally</li>
        <li>Full party healing occurs at the <strong>start of each new Act</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Relic Drafting -->
    <section id="relic-drafting" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">5. Relic Drafting</h2>

      <p>
        When the team opens a chest (or defeats an elite), the game presents <strong>one relic per player</strong>.
        If two players want the same relic, a <strong>rock-paper-scissors</strong> tiebreaker decides who gets it.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2 not-prose">Drafting Strategy</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-1 mt-3">
        <li><strong>Communicate before clicking.</strong> Don't let the fastest clicker grab everything</li>
        <li>Give Strength/Damage relics to your DPS</li>
        <li>Give Block/HP relics to your tank</li>
        <li>Give Energy/Utility relics to your debuffer or orb character</li>
        <li>Avoid duplicate classes — they compete for the same class-specific relics, effectively halving your team's relic income</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: Map Voting -->
    <section id="map-voting" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">6. Map Voting &amp; Pathing</h2>

      <p>
        In co-op, the team votes on which path to take. Ties are broken randomly. You can draw on the map to suggest routes to your team.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2 not-prose">Pathing Tips</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-1 mt-3">
        <li>If one player is struggling with low HP, prioritize a <strong>Rest Site</strong> over an Elite fight</li>
        <li><strong>Negotiate</strong> rather than forcing selfish routes</li>
        <li>Take <strong>elites early</strong> — the relic payoff is multiplied in co-op</li>
        <li>The Golden Compass (Act 2 Tezcatara boon) replaces the map with a single linear path the whole party must follow</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 7: Co-op Exclusive Cards -->
    <section id="coop-cards" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">7. Co-op Exclusive Cards</h2>

      <p>
        Every character has multiplayer-exclusive cards that <strong>do not appear in solo mode</strong>.
        These cards create team synergies that transform how you build decks.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 my-4">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Rally</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">ALL players gain 12 Block. One of the most universally useful co-op cards.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Coordinate</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Give another player +5 Strength this turn. Enables devastating coordinated attacks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Gang Up</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Deals bonus damage for each time another player attacked that enemy this turn.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Beacon of Hope</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Whenever you gain Block, other players gain half as much. Turns tanks into team protectors.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Intercept</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Gain 9 Block and redirect all attacks from a teammate to yourself. Clutch save tool.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Flanking</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Targeted enemy takes double damage from other players for the rest of the turn. (Silent exclusive)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Lift</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Give another player 11 Block. Simple but efficient protection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        <a href="/coop/card-synergies/" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline font-semibold">
          See the full co-op card synergies guide &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 8: 10 Essential Tips -->
    <section id="essential-tips" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">8. 10 Essential Multiplayer Tips</h2>

      <div class="space-y-4 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 1: Build a Balanced Party</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Coordinate roles before the run starts. Don't run four glass cannons. Aim for at least one tank and one debuffer. Ironclad (tank) + Silent (debuffer) is the safest starting pair for new co-op players.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 2: Slow Down &amp; Coordinate Plays</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Everyone acts simultaneously. Use voice chat. Call out debuffs first — don't waste damage before Vulnerable is applied.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 3: Debuffs Benefit Everyone</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Apply Vulnerable and Weak at the start of every turn. Poison and Doom bypass Block and work across the entire team. This is the single highest-impact mechanic in co-op.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 4: Communicate Relic Picks</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">When chests open, talk through who gets each relic. Match relics to roles — Strength to DPS, Block to tank. Don't fight over the same relic; it wastes team potential.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 5: Draft Multiplayer-Specific Cards</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Co-op exclusive cards (Rally, Intercept, Flanking, etc.) are often run-defining. They don't appear in solo mode, so don't skip them out of habit.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 6: Throw Potions on Teammates</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Throwing potions can heal or buff allies in trouble. Save them for clutch moments — a well-timed thrown potion can save a run.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 7: Build Synergies Across the Team</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Certain class pairings excel beyond the sum of their parts. Ironclad + Silent covers everything. Necrobinder + Regent has the highest damage ceiling. See our <a href="/coop/character-combos/" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">Character Combos guide</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 8: Have a Designated Survivor</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">As long as one player survives, everyone revives. Your tankiest character should play conservatively when the team is low. Funnel defensive resources to them.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 9: Choose Your Map Path Wisely</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Vote with the team's collective health in mind. If a teammate is struggling, a Rest Site is worth more than an Elite. Negotiate — don't force selfish routes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400">Tip 10: Play More to Unlock</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1">Progress in co-op unlocks new Epochs, cards, relics, and potions — just like solo play. Complete solo runs on the side to practice characters and unlock more options for multiplayer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Quick Do's and Don'ts -->
    <section class="mt-10 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4">Quick Do's and Don'ts</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="bg-green-900/20 border border-green-700/40 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-400 mb-2">✅ DO</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-green-300 space-y-1">
            <li>Assign roles (tank, debuffer, DPS) before Act 1</li>
            <li>Stack debuffs on turn 1 before the team unloads damage</li>
            <li>Take Elites early — relic value is multiplied in co-op</li>
            <li>Use the host with the best wired internet</li>
            <li>Communicate relic picks before clicking</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-red-900/20 border border-red-700/40 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-red-400 mb-2">❌ DON'T</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-red-300 space-y-1">
            <li>Run duplicate characters — relic competition kills efficiency</li>
            <li>Play with mods enabled — they cause desyncs in co-op</li>
            <li>Ignore multiplayer-specific cards in rewards</li>
            <li>Attack before debuffs are applied</li>
            <li>Force selfish map routes when teammates need Rest Sites</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <!-- Next page link -->
  <div class="not-prose mt-12 text-center">
    <p class="text-slate-400 mb-3">Continue reading:</p>
    <a href="/coop/character-combos/" class="inline-block bg-amber-600 hover:bg-amber-500 text-black font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors">
      Character Combos: Best Team Compositions &rarr;
    </a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
